# Digests of specification revisions AS DEPOSITED.
#
# Each line records the exact bytes published under a document's DOI for one
# version string. Written at deposit time, never edited afterwards: a published
# revision is immutable, so its digest is too.
#
# The rule this file enforces, checked by tools/check_spec_versioning.py on every
# verification pass:
#
#     If a document's current version string appears here, the file in this
#     repository MUST hash to the digest recorded for it. Otherwise the version
#     string MUST be bumped.
#
# In other words a version string is never reused for different bytes. The
# repository copy may legitimately run ahead of the deposited copy — that is how
# the next revision is prepared — but it must then carry the next version
# string, so "the 1.0.0-draft.1 text" can only ever mean one sequence of bytes
# no matter which copy you are holding.
#
# That is what makes the precedence rule in each document's Status section
# mechanically checkable rather than a promise: the deposit governs, and if a
# copy claims the same version string, it is either identical or the build fails.
#
# Format:  <filename>  <version>  <sha256>
#
# No revision has been deposited yet. Entries appear here when the Zenodo
# deposits are published.
